got this yummy treat  oh my goodness leroy  oh my gosh lieutenant dan  come here hey danny  hi i'm vanessa a pastry chef and i'm  also a crazy dog mom for my little  puppy's birthday i made homemade dog  safe birthday treats and i'm going to  show you how to make them for your own  fur baby let's get started of course you  know your fur baby best so use  discretion when serving just in case  they might have a sensitive tummy so  what we're going to do is we're gonna  add our ingredients to our stand mixer  we're gonna add half a cup of peanut  butter and four eggs  and next we're gonna add a cup and a  half of sweet potato puree you wanna  blend this nice and smooth before you  add your flour  okay this looks perfectly smooth enough  for us to add our six cups of whole  wheat flour this looks a little too  sticky and we want a nice soft ball to  be able to roll it out so i'm going to  add a little bit more whole wheat flour  to get it to a nice consistency you  don't have to use all six cups if you  see that it's coming together with less  amount of flour  this mixture has had enough  perfect this is a nice soft ball of  dough not too sticky it all came  together really well i only ended up  using about four cups so you can adjust  as needed okay this is a beautiful piece  of dough i'm so excited it's nice and  soft great consistency i'm gonna use a  little bit of flour for my board and a  little bit of flour on top  so i'm gonna roll this out to about half  an inch thick so we've got our dog  biscuit cutter because obviously and  this should yield about two dozen dog  biscuits these are so freaking cute  i love this what a fun idea for like  birthday parties definitely great gift  ideas for your dog friends or your  friends that have dogs  [Laughter]  when these bake these are going to be  kind of firm like a traditional dog  biscuit this peanut butter smells so  good i want one of these for myself and  while we're waiting i'm going to show  you how to jazz it up with a peanut  butter drizzle sauce for our peanut  butter drizzle it's just half a cup of  peanut butter  and two tablespoons of coconut oil we're  going to melt this down on a medium heat  on the stove until it all comes together  so this is more about melting than it is  about cooking it looks about done so i'm  gonna check on our dog biscuits and then  we'll finish our dog treats i let them  cool to the touch for about 15 minutes  we've got our biscuits we've got our  peanut butter drizzle now let's decorate  so our peanut butter drizzle is nice and  cool great consistency for drizzling  this drizzle just kind of jazzes up your  biscuits a little bit gives it a real  michelin feel this is so cute  these biscuits look so irresistible if  your dog doesn't love these you need to  take him to the vet a fork is also easy  to use if you want to have that nice  professional drizzled look all righty  these are done we've got our first treat  for our puppy party next we're gonna  make a carrot peanut butter spice cake  so we're gonna start by mixing our dry  ingredients together we've got one cup  of whole wheat flour one teaspoon of  cinnamon one teaspoon of ginger and a  teaspoon and a half of baking powder  we're just going to mix these together  until they're nice and incorporated so  next we're going to work on our wet  ingredients we have two eggs we have one  third of a cup of applesauce three  tablespoons of honey one tablespoon of  molasses half a cup of peanut butter and  we're also going to add a quarter of a  cup of vegetable oil we're going to give  this a nice mix so we mix our dry and  wet ingredients separately that way our  dry ingredients are incorporated fully  and we don't over mix our batter okay so  this is nice and mixed now we're going  to combine the two together make sure  that you scrape your sides you want to  get all of your ingredients in your  batter it's going to start to thicken as  you mix it our last ingredient is going  to be one cup of finely grated carrots  which we're gonna fold in so this is  done and keeping in the theme of our  biscuits we have a dog-shaped cake pan  so now we're gonna add our batter into  our dog bone cake pan this has already  been  pre-greased that way it doesn't stick to  the cake pan and it pops right out in a  perfect shape you want to spread it  evenly into the pan that way the cake  bakes evenly just like the dog biscuits  we're gonna put this in the oven on 350  for 20 to 25 minutes and then when we  come back i'll show you how to put the  icing on the cake except that it's  frosting  our dog frosting is two ingredients 16  ounces of cream cheese and three  tablespoons of honey we're gonna give  this a nice paddle so it's nice and  smooth  i'm noticing this isn't the exact  consistency that i want so we're just  going to add a little bit of water to  smooth it out to give it a better  consistency  [Applause]  okay this is perfect let's go get our  cakes and complete our puppy party so  first we're going to decorate our dog  cake i'm gonna get our dog friendly  frosting and put it on top and we're  gonna get some on the sides as well i'm  using a large offset spatula just to  spoon it on top and i'm gonna use a  small offset spatula to get into the  grooves using a small offset spatula is  great for when you're decorating small  cakes when you have different shapes and  different crevices because it's really  going to help you get right into the  details of things i'm doing a sweeping  motion of backwards forwards to evenly  spread my frosting i'm also making sure  that i'm using the frosting to get a  nice even coating on the cake so at my  dog puppy party i coated my cake and  fondant but this is much more at home  cook based base user-friendly so that's  why i definitely recommend using a  buttercream over fondant all right so we  are done i'm just gonna do what we did  with our dog biscuits and just do a fun  peanut butter drizzle  okay so that's it that's our puppy cake  okay guys there we have it we have our  dog friendly cake and of course the  delicious dog biscuit treats now you're  ready to be the perfect dog parents that  you've always dreamed  come here penny  is that yummy  let us know in the comments if you want  to see any more homemade pet recipes and  i'll see you next time oh yes  [Music]  [Music]  you

